  <diagram id="4-ZktouHjqXsSP9FziCv" name="3-Questions-Assumptions">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1373" dy="703" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="IacCic1ztX3TOTFWdiGO-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h3&gt;1. Questions&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="100" x="20" y="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="IacCic1ztX3TOTFWdiGO-2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&#xa;&lt;ol start=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;[SRS 7.1]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; Can an employee manage different branches at different periods, and can a branch manager temporarily manage more than one branch during an emergency?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;[SRS 7.1]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; Are middle names and company email addresses mandatory for every employee, and can an employee have more than one company email?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;[SRS 7.2]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; What is the minimum passing score for a course, and can an employee retake a course after passing it?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;[SRS 7.3]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; When a vehicle has a model-specific rate, does that rate always override the category rate, and can the model-specific rate also change over time?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;[SRS 7.7, 8]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; How should a person who is both an individual customer and a company&#39;s authorized driver be represented without duplicating their identity?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;[SRS 7.8]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; Can the same corporate contract have multiple discounts for the same vehicle category during different periods, and are overlapping periods prohibited?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;[SRS 7.9]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; Does the maximum number of promotion uses apply globally or separately to each customer or branch?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;[SRS 7.10]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; How many points are earned or redeemed per rental, and what is the exact rule for calculating the points balance after refunds or rental cancellations?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;[SRS 7.12]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; Can a corporate rental have multiple drivers, and must the main driver always be selected from that corporate customer&#39;s authorized-driver list?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;[SRS 7.12, 7.16]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; How are late fees, damage charges, and traffic fines calculated, and can they be paid through separate payment transactions?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;[SRS 7.16]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; How are corporate monthly invoices finalized, and how should payments made by a corporate customer be allocated across its rentals?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;[SRS 7.5, 10]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; Since real-time GPS tracking is out of scope, how will the system satisfy the objective of knowing the location of every vehicle at all times?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xa;&#xa;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="420" width="970" x="20" y="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="IacCic1ztX3TOTFWdiGO-3" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h3&gt;2. Assumptions&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="110" x="20" y="540" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="IacCic1ztX3TOTFWdiGO-4" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;ol start=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.1]&lt;/strong&gt; A surrogate AssignmentID is used as the primary key for BranchManagerAssignment because the SRS does not specify an identifier for each management assignment period.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.1]&lt;/strong&gt; A nullable EndDate is used to record when a manager&#39;s assignment ends. A NULL EndDate means the assignment is still active.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.2]&lt;/strong&gt; Each course attempt is identified by EmployeeID, CourseCode, and AttemptNo, allowing the system to preserve every attempt made by an employee.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.3]&lt;/strong&gt; A separate CarModelRate entity is used for model-specific pricing. A model-specific rate takes precedence over its category rate when applicable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.3]&lt;/strong&gt; CurrentBranchCode represents the last known operational branch of a vehicle. It does not represent its live GPS location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.5]&lt;/strong&gt; VIN in GPSDevice is nullable because a device may remain in the warehouse without being installed in a vehicle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.7]&lt;/strong&gt; Customer is modeled as a supertype with IndividualCustomer and CorporateCustomer as mutually exclusive subtypes, following the statement that every customer is one kind or the other.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.7]&lt;/strong&gt; AuthorizedDriver is modeled as a weak entity identified by CorporateCustomerNo and DriverNo because each company&#39;s driver numbers are meaningful only within that company.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.8]&lt;/strong&gt; CorporateContractDiscount uses a separate DiscountID because the same contract may have multiple discount records for the same category during different periods.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.10]&lt;/strong&gt; Loyalty points balance and customer tier are derived from recorded point movements rather than manually stored values.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.12]&lt;/strong&gt; ReservationNo is nullable in Rental because walk-in rentals do not originate from reservations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.12]&lt;/strong&gt; ReceivingAgentID is nullable until the vehicle is returned because the receiving employee is not known at pickup time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.12]&lt;/strong&gt; PreviousRentalID is a nullable self-referencing foreign key used to represent rental extensions as a chain of rental agreements.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.14]&lt;/strong&gt; DamageReport is identified by RentalID and ReportNumber because report numbers restart for each rental.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.14]&lt;/strong&gt; FeedbackID is used as a surrogate primary key, while RentalID is unique to enforce at most one feedback record per rental.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.15]&lt;/strong&gt; JobMechanic, JobPart, and SupplierPart are separate associative tables to represent their many-to-many relationships and store relationship-specific attributes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.16]&lt;/strong&gt; CorporateInvoice is linked to CorporateCustomer and Rental through InvoiceID in Rental. One invoice represents one corporate customer&#39;s billing period.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.16]&lt;/strong&gt; Payment transaction references are optional at the column level because cash payments have no reference, while card and bank transfer payments require one.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="640" width="890" x="60" y="570" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="IacCic1ztX3TOTFWdiGO-5" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h3&gt;3. Contradictions&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="130" x="20" y="1250" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="IacCic1ztX3TOTFWdiGO-6" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;ol start=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 7.7 vs. SRS 8 – Customer Identity]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Section 7.7 states that every customer is either an individual customer or a corporate customer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Section 8 states that some corporate authorized drivers are also individual customers who rent vehicles for personal use.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;These statements create an identity-modeling conflict: a person may need to act in both roles, although the customer classification is described as mutually exclusive.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 5 (Objective O-1), 7.5 and 10 – Vehicle Location Tracking]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Objective O-1 requires knowing the location of every vehicle at all times.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Section 7.5 describes GPS tracking devices, but Section 10 explicitly excludes the real-time GPS tracking dashboard from Phase 1 and includes only device registration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;The full real-time location objective cannot be achieved by device registration alone within the stated Phase 1 scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[SRS 9 (NFR-1) vs. SRS 8 – Rental Check-out Performance]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;NFR-1 requires rental check-out to complete in under 3 seconds of system time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Section 8 states that check-out should not take more than 3 minutes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;The two sections specify significantly different performance targets and should be clarified by the business stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="390" width="960" x="50" y="1270" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="lxsqwz8nTnLr2tidkZ2r" name=" 4-Business-Rules">
    <mxGraphModel dx="2387" dy="1887" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="qY4Exsxz0f0CBXDSNQYs-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&#xa;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;SRS Section:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; 7.10 – Loyalty Program&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Business Rule:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;A customer&#39;s loyalty tier must always be calculated from the customer&#39;s current points balance:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Silver: below 1,000 points.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Gold: from 1,000 to 4,999 points.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Platinum: 5,000 points and above.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;The points balance must reflect all earned and redeemed point movements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Why constraints are not enough:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;The tier depends on the aggregate result of multiple loyalty point movement records. PK, FK, NOT NULL, UNIQUE, CHECK, and DEFAULT constraints cannot independently maintain this aggregate balance and its corresponding tier whenever movements are added or changed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;How to enforce it:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Use a database trigger or stored procedure to update the points balance and determine the tier whenever a loyalty point movement is recorded. Alternatively, calculate the balance and tier dynamically in the application from the complete movement history.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&#xa;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="470" width="840" y="-170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qY4Exsxz0f0CBXDSNQYs-2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SRS Section:&lt;/strong&gt; 7.7, 7.12 and 7.16 – Customers, Rentals and Payments&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Rule:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Every corporate rental must be assigned to a monthly invoice belonging to the same corporate customer. An invoice must not contain rentals belonging to another corporate customer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why constraints are not enough:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A foreign key can verify that InvoiceID exists, but it cannot by itself guarantee that the corporate customer associated with the rental is the same customer associated with the invoice. This requires comparing data across related tables.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to enforce it:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Use a database trigger or a stored procedure when inserting or updating a rental or invoice assignment. Verify that the rental&#39;s corporate customer matches the invoice&#39;s CorporateCustomerNo before accepting the operation.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="540" width="820" x="-20" y="230" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
